<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Regulating Act of 1773</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1773">1773</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as East India Company Act 1772</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Regulating Act of 1773 was the first act of the British Parliament to regulate the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>'s government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. It created the post of governor-general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, first held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warren-hastings">Warren Hastings</a>, with a council of four and authority over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Madras</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mumbai">Bombay</a>, and set up a Supreme Court at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolkata">Calcutta</a>. Pitt's India Act of 1784 extended this control.</p></div>
